"""
Bloom — Healthy Habits App  (rewritten Flet framework)
======================================================

Key improvements in this version
--------------------------------
1. Every food lookup and photo analysis runs in a BACKGROUND THREAD with a
   modal LOADING screen, so the UI never freezes. The loading screen for a
   typed food stays up until the nutrition tab has actually been updated.
2. Photo upload shows its own loading screen, then asks the user to CONFIRM
   the matched food. If they say it's wrong, they're prompted to type the
   correct food name, which is then logged like a normal entry.
3. The CLIP model + text-embedding matrix are loaded ONCE and cached
   (in-memory + on disk), instead of being rebuilt on every photo.
4. All hard-coded Windows paths are gone — CSVs / checkpoints are resolved
   relative to this file (BASE_DIR), so the app is portable.
5. Heavy ML deps (torch / open_clip / cv2 / numpy / PIL / SAM / Depth) are
   imported lazily and wrapped in guards, so the app still runs (and the
   typed-food path still works) even if the vision stack isn't installed.

Expected files next to this script (BASE_DIR):
    food.csv           (columns: fdc_id, description)
    food_nutrient.csv  (columns: fdc_id, nutrient_id, amount)
    nutrient.csv       (columns: nutrient_nbr, name)         # optional
    checkpoints/sam2_hiera_small.pt                          # optional
    checkpoints/depth_anything_v2_vits.pth                   # optional

Install / run:
    pip install flet
    # optional, for photo analysis:
    pip install torch open_clip_torch opencv-python pillow numpy
    export ANTHROPIC_API_KEY="sk-ant-..."
    python bloom_app.py
"""

